{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTeKWEeem9eVHHUUDyFe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Replay of what's settled, then the reading I'll draw from.\n\n**Settled from your answers (all still assumed, since no source backs them)**\n- **Reader and outcome:** the Roamstay Product team, agreeing how date changes behave, with the three price results as the part that must read first\n- **Dials:** Balanced detail, Mixed audience, Laptop distance\n- **Left out:** cancellation, payment failure, host-side screens, and change-window and fee rules\n\n**The question and the outcome**\n- **Question:** what does a guest go through to change booking dates, and what does the new price do to them?\n- **Outcome:** the team can see every path to the updated booking and agree what happens in each price case\n\n**What the request settled:** every node and these edges come straight from your wording. They are the Change dates tap and date pick, \"not free\" leading to other rooms, the three price results, and the updated booking at the end.\n\n**What I inferred**\n- **The \"free\" exit:** a free room goes straight to the price check. The request never says so, but nothing else can follow\n- **After other rooms:** the guest picks a room and lands at the same price check. The request ends at \"they see other rooms\", so this is my reading. Another next step, such as going back to the dates or leaving the flow, would change the board\n- **Actors:** the guest taps and picks, and the app checks the room, takes the payment and issues the credit\n- **Source class:** current behavior, with your request as the only source\n\n**Outline (drawing order, 9 nodes, 11 connectors)**\n1. The board answers: what does a Roamstay guest go through to change booking dates, and what does the new price do to them?\n2. Booking page (start), then \"Tap Change dates\" to Pick new dates, so the tap is a connector label and not a node\n3. Pick new dates, then \"Room free on those dates?\"\n4. Room free on those dates?, Yes to the price check and No to See other rooms\n5. See other rooms, \"Pick a room\" to the price check (assumed)\n6. New price vs current?, Higher to Pay the difference, Lower to Get the difference as credit, and Same to the merge dot labelled \"Same, nothing charged\"\n7. Pay the difference and Get the difference as credit each go to the merge dot\n8. Merge dot, then Updated booking (end)\n\n**Two framings**\n- **Spine with branches beside it (recommended):** Booking page to Updated booking runs straight, with the other-rooms detour and the three price branches beside it. It stays at 9 nodes, but the detour reads as a side trip\n- **Outcome map:** one end per price result. It shows each result as its own finish, but it needs two more nodes, so it goes over 9 and splits into two boards\n\n**The look (recommended choices)**\n- **Accent:** the price check, because that is the part that must read first. The goal, Updated booking, is named but not styled\n- **Zones:** none. Nine nodes on one spine read without grouping, and the accent already guides the eye\n- **Title:** Change booking dates\n- **Subtitle:** How a Roamstay guest changes the dates on a booking, and what the new price does to them\n- **Source line:** Sources: a written description of the app flow. Left out: cancellation, payment failure, host-side screens, change-window and fee rules.\n\nIs this reading right, with \"Pick a room\" as the step after the guest sees other rooms?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5091,"cache_read_input_tokens":85134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5091},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58